Third-party software
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project builds and runs vanitygen, which is a separate program under a
different licence:

    vanitygen
    Copyright (C) 2011 samr7 <samr7@cs.washington.edu>
    https://github.com/samr7/vanitygen
    GNU Affero General Public License, version 3

vanitygen's source is NOT included in this repository. scripts/build-vanitygen.sh
clones it from upstream at a pinned commit (cd1a7282431dcf7e522777976aa18728ee5bb7be),
applies vendor/patches/, and builds it. It is executed as a separate process and
is never linked into this software, so the two licences remain separate.

vendor/patches/0001-openssl3-pcre2.patch is a modification of vanitygen and is
therefore itself licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3, as
stated in its header. It is published here so that anyone else building
vanitygen against OpenSSL 3.x may use it. It contains:

  1. the changes needed to compile against OpenSSL 3.x and PCRE2;
  2. a fix for a crash after a successful match, caused by worker threads that
     were never joined;
  3. a fix for prefixes with exactly three leading "1" characters failing to
     match at one of their two possible Base58 rendering lengths.

Items 2 and 3 are defects in vanitygen itself rather than artefacts of the
port. Upstream has been dormant since 2013.

